# Animation Module

## Purpose

Frame-based sprite animation. `AnimationSystem` loads and caches shared `AnimationClip` assets; per-entity playback state lives in `AnimatedSpriteComponent`. Each frame, `AnimationSystem::Update()` advances playing components and writes `texture_index` into `RenderComponent`. All frame textures are bindless PNGs registered at clip load time.

## Key Types

| Type | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| `AnimatedSpriteComponent` | Per-entity playback state: `clip_id`, frame index, elapsed time, playing/loop/finished flags |
| `AnimationSystem` | Clip cache (`LoadClip`), playback API, per-frame `Update()` tick |

## API

```cpp
// Load once, share across entities (deduped by path)
ResourceId clip_id = animation_system.LoadClip( render_system, "path/to/animation.json" );

// Attach to entity (must already have RenderComponent)
animation_system.Attach( entity, clip_id );

// Playback control
animation_system.ShowFrame( entity, 0 );
animation_system.PauseEntity( entity );
animation_system.Play( entity, 0 );       // play from frame 0
animation_system.PlayOnce( entity, 0 );   // one-shot from frame 0
animation_system.SetLoop( entity, true );

// Poll state
if( animation_system.IsFinished( entity ) ) { /* one-shot done */ }

// Called once per frame from VortexGame (after PhysicsSystem::Update)
animation_system.Update( delta_time_sec );
```

## How It Works

1. `AnimationSystem::LoadClip()` calls `AnimationClip::Load()` and caches the result by JSON path.
2. `Attach()` adds `AnimatedSpriteComponent` with the clip `ResourceId`, shows frame 0, and pauses.
3. `Update()` accumulates `delta_time_sec` into `elapsed` for each playing component.
4. When `elapsed >= frame.duration_sec`, advance to the next frame (reset elapsed).
5. Write the new frame's `texture_index` into `registry.GetComponent<RenderComponent>( entity )`.
6. At end-of-clip: loop back to frame 0 if `loop == true`, else hold last frame, set `playing = false`, `finished = true`.

## Key Patterns

- **Requires `RenderComponent`:** The entity must have a `RenderComponent` before `Attach()`. Missing component -> no texture write.
- **Shared clip, per-entity component:** Load one clip via `LoadClip()`, attach to many entities with the same `ResourceId`.
- **One component per entity:** Each `AnimatedSpriteComponent` tracks its own timer state.

## DOs

- Call `AnimationSystem::Update()` every frame from the main loop -- missing frames causes visible hitches
- Pair animated entities with `RenderSystem::AttachSprite()` / `AttachRenderable()` using frame 0's texture index and clip frame size
- Use `ShowFrame( 0 )` + `PauseEntity()` to display a static frame while the entity is alive (e.g. pooled bullets)

## DON'Ts

- Don't manually write `RenderComponent::texture_index` while an `AnimatedSpriteComponent` is playing -- it will be overwritten on the next `Update()`
- Don't attach animation before the entity has a `RenderComponent`
- Don't store `AnimationClip` on scene classes -- use `AnimationSystem::LoadClip()` instead
